        "id": 106074,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-09T15:59:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The story arc where Omnitron assimilates Omnitron-X to becomes Omnitron 4 (presumably) is called \"Singularity\"</p><p>A Wrath player with a small deck and an OCS Waypoint plotter can endlessly loop through her deck while moving and re-positioning every other ship on the table. She is devestatingly powerfull when built this way as you can take the threat of an overrun loss totally off the table. I always thought Sensor Array should have been limited to the first time you move each phase, but thats not how the card ended up. Wrath is the Legacy of the base set SF ships.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:35:52.338Z",
